list.t:
resolve the Node Descriptor identified by the keyid URL with its
fragment removed (), and verify that the key is listed in
authentication and has not been revoked ();

reject the message if created is more than 60 seconds in the
future, if the current time is more than 60 seconds after
expires, or if expires minus created exceeds 300 seconds;

if the object hash is identical, the receiver MUST respond 202
with an Ack whose status is "duplicate", and MUST NOT process it
again;

viewable time MUST be reported only as viewableSeconds sums in
aggregate cells; per-render times MUST NOT be reported to any other
party or retained after the batch is issued;

the k-threshold of  applies to the cell's count: a
cell whose count is below k MUST be merged before its
viewableSeconds is reported;

resolve host names and refuse connections to loopback, private,
link-local, unique-local, multicast and other special-purpose
addresses, re-checking after each redirect;
